{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1268","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Happy Cactus"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"3 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given a cactus graph, in this graph each edge lies on at most one simple cycle."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is given as $$$m$$$ edges $$$a_i, b_i$$$, weight of $$$i$$$-th edge is $$$i$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's call a path in cactus "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"increasing"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if the weights of edges on this path are increasing."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's call a pair of vertices $$$(u,v)$$$ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"happy"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if there exists an increasing path that starts in $$$u$$$ and ends in $$$v$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each vertex $$$u$$$ find the number of other vertices $$$v$$$, such that pair $$$(u,v)$$$ is happy."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of input contains two integers $$$n,m$$$ ($$$1 \\leq n, m \\leq 500\\,000$$$): the number of vertices and edges in the given cactus."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The next $$$m$$$ lines contain a description of cactus edges, $$$i$$$-th of them contain two integers $$$a_i, b_i$$$ ($$$1 \\leq a_i, b_i \\leq n, a_i \\neq b_i$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that there are no multiple edges and the graph is connected."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print $$$n$$$ integers, required values for vertices $$$1,2,\\ldots,n$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3 3\n1 2\n2 3\n3 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2 2 2 \n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5 4\n1 2\n2 3\n3 4\n4 5\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4 4 3 2 1 \n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"1268E","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1268/problem/E"}